          "text": "{\"locale\":\"en\",\"answer\":\"No. An observation gap alone does not justify concluding that an object does not exist. It shows only that current evidence cannot reliably distinguish the target; limited resolution, observation range, or time window may leave the object unknown. Non-observation is not equivalent to nonexistence.\",\"supportMap\":[{\"statement\":\"No. An observation gap alone does not justify concluding that an object does not exist.\",\"sourceIds\":[\"S1\"],\"relation\":\"DIRECT_SUPPORT\"},{\"statement\":\"It shows only that current evidence cannot reliably distinguish the target; limited resolution, observation range, or time window may leave the object unknown.\",\"sourceIds\":[\"S1\"],\"relation\":\"DIRECT_SUPPORT\"},{\"statement\":\"Non-observation is not equivalent to nonexistence.\",\"sourceIds\":[\"S1\"],\"relation\":\"DIRECT_SUPPORT\"}],\"limitations\":\"The evidence does not establish that the object exists; it establishes only that non-observation is insufficient to conclude that it does not exist.\"}"
